# Decisions

Purpose:
  Central decision ledger. Every human and AI decision gets a written record.
  If it's not in the decision ledger, it didn't happen.

Owns: ./

Types:
  architectural: Architecture decisions
  technical: Tech stack choices
  security: Security decisions
  business: Business rule decisions
  operational: Deployment/ops decisions
  human: Human approvals/rejections
  ai: AI proposals/decisions

ReadOrder:
   1  @schema.sdd
   2  @workflow.sdd
   3  @rules.sdd

Files:
  schema: @schema.sdd
  workflow: @workflow.sdd
  rules: @rules.sdd
  project: @project/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [DR1] Every decision MUST have a unique ID (DEC-XXX).
  [DR2] Every decision MUST have a type.
  [DR3] Every decision MUST have at least 2 options.
  [DR4] Every decision MUST have an owner.
  [DR5] AI MAY create decisions for technical choices.
  [DR6] Human MUST create architectural/security/business decisions.
  [DR7] Architectural decisions require human approval.
  [DR8] Security decisions require human approval.
  [DR9] Business decisions require human approval.
  [DR10] Technical decisions MAY be auto-approved.
  [DR11] All approvals MUST be recorded with timestamp.
  [DR12] Rejections MUST include feedback.
  [DR13] Implemented decisions MUST reference task IDs.
  [DR14] Verified decisions MUST have passing criteria.
  [DR15] Superseded decisions MUST reference new decision.
  [DR16] Conflicting decisions MUST be flagged.
  [DR17] Decision history MUST be preserved.
  [DR18] All decisions MUST be indexed in INDEX.sdd.
  [DR19] Active decisions MUST be easily discoverable.
  [DR20] Decision rationale MUST be accessible to AI.
  [DW1] Every significant change MUST have a decision record.
  [DW2] Architectural decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW3] Security decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW4] AI MAY propose technical decisions.
  [DW5] Human MAY override AI decisions.
  [DW6] Superseded decisions MUST reference new decision.
  [DW7] Conflicting decisions MUST be resolved before implementation.
  [DW8] Decision rationale MUST be recorded.
  [DW9] Implementation MUST reference decision ID.
  [DW10] Verification MUST reference decision criteria.
  [DTL1] Every approved decision MUST create at least one task.
  [DTL2] Every task MUST reference its parent decision.
  [DTL3] Decision status MUST update as tasks progress.
  [DTL4] Verification MUST run before decision is closed.
  [DTL5] Superseded decisions MUST migrate tasks to new decision.

State: +